WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.780
So the sportswriter
came in and he

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.710
said, listen, man, I haven't
seen a performance like that

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.300
ever in my life.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.950
He says, I want to
give you a nickname.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.750
Earvin, we got to
call you something.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.810
Somebody's called Biggie,
somebody's called Dr. Jay.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.460
How about Magic?

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.260
You know, you're
like, yeah, right.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.050
[LAUGHS] You start
laughing like,

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:23.750
OK, my boy is not
going to call me Magic.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.320
And within two months.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.920
Everybody in Michigan
knew who Magic was.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.907
And I had heard about this kid,
you know, Earvin Magic Johnson.

00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:39.990
I was like, who's this
dude, Earvin Magic Johnson?

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.390
Never saw him but just
kept hearing how great he

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.010
was as a basketball player.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.410
Now, he goes,
watch it, could be.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:46.420
He slams it--

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:49.450
Have you seen this
kid in Lansing?

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:53.650
This 15-year-old Black
kid from the Midwest.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:54.490
They call him Magic.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:55.510
Have you seen him?

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.090
Earvin Johnson, you're a
very sought after player.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:01.570
You shoot well, you pass well,
you dribble, score assist.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.335
We trying to figure
out what you do best.

00:01:03.335 --> 00:01:03.835
Do you know?

00:01:03.835 --> 00:01:05.379
We can't figure it out.

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:07.930
When the newspapers really
start getting involved

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.330
and then start getting
the big headlines,

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.250
you know, that's
when he basically

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:13.870
became the pied piper.

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:17.050
Whatever game he was playing,
everybody wanted to go see it.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:21.632
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.380
Everywhere we would go, you
could not find a seat anyplace.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.000
You just could not find a seat.

